*   Try-with-resources is mainly used to automatically close resources (files, streams, database connections, etc.). It is not specifically an exception-handling mechanism.
         ~However, exceptions can still occur inside try-with-resources, and you can use catch or throws to handle/propagate them.

*   Try-with-resources ke saath 3 possibilities hain:

    1. Only try-with-resources
    try (FileReader file = new FileReader("a.txt")) {
        // code
    }


    2. try-with-resources + catch
    try (FileReader file = new FileReader("a.txt")) {
        // code
    } catch (IOException e) {
        System.out.println("File error");
    }



    3. try-with-resources + finally
    try (FileReader file = new FileReader("a.txt")) {
        // code
    } finally {
        // code
    }